# ⛔ THE BUILD CONTEXT MUST NOT CARRY THE HOST'S node_modules.
#
# web.Dockerfile installs workspace deps into the image FIRST (for layer caching) and only then
# does `COPY apps/web/ apps/web/`. With no ignore file that COPY overwrote the container's freshly
# installed `apps/web/node_modules` with whatever the host happened to have — a partial, pnpm-hoisted
# tree with no `typescript` at that level — and the build died on:
#
#     Error: Cannot find module '/app/apps/web/node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc'
#
# So `make up` failed on any machine that had ever run `pnpm install`, and succeeded on CI, which
# never had. Host state leaking into an image build is the whole failure mode a build context is
# supposed to prevent.
#
# ⚠ DELIBERATELY NARROW. Nothing else is excluded — not `.git`, not `dist` — because this file
# applies to EVERY image (api, node, migrate, operator, web) and a broader ignore risks silently
# starving a build that legitimately reads those paths. Add entries one at a time, with a reason.
**/node_modules
